 "structural_change": "S81-TOPK4 ACC32 + REGIONAL CLOCK K8 (10-19 23:05): RTL = s81dvbk_sq_succ3 (FAN32+ACC32, d72e81e31); clock = physical/common_flow/clock_split_km.tcl K 8 (one local root per placed register-mass centroid, beside its SRAM stack, one top tree). Why: succ3 gate (agidock 20261019-213502) single 42k-sink tree -> post-CTS FF hold ws -109.3 / tns -56.3k on 12,968 endpoints (flop->flop pipelines g_cst/cp/wdata, intra-tile skew; QDM all-sink skew 90+), hold repair stagnating at -87.3 (gate-stall risk, as succ1 / sq_reg); sq_reg (FAN32 + K16, no ACC32) measured FF hold ws -38.9 / tns -3.2k and pin-flop range TT 578.9..588.4 (9.5 ps), its only blocker was the packer acc setup that ACC32 removes (succ3 placed TT WNS +27.4, 0 violating endpoints). Crossings between regions stay register-to-register on one phase-0 port, tile 324x540 (<405 um per hop): 0 added edges.",
